      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(store): order hydration observations durably",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- order canonical thread state, accepted evidence, child hydration, and workflow-run snapshots by GitHub source revision before local pre-fetch generation\n- allow a delayed newer source snapshot to replace an older snapshot even when it allocated a lower local generation\n- reject delayed stale hydration before it overwrites comments, PR details, documents, summaries, embeddings, or cluster inputs\n- converge supported schema-4/6/8/9/10 stores to one canonical schema with atomic rollback, exact stored-DDL checks, and a byte-stable healthy-v10 fast path\n- reject and repair the unrepresentable minimum-int64 observation sequence\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated at `506e084`:\n\n- `go test ./... -count=1`\n- `go test -race ./... -count=1`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...`\n- `make generate-sqlc` followed by a clean generated diff\n- `go mod tidy` followed by a clean module diff\n- `make test-coverage`: total coverage `85.0%`\n- equal-tuple subset/superset ordering, populated-baseline same-generation verified-deletion sibling ordering, commit-time deletion CAS, and accepted-evidence archive coverage adversarial tests repeated `100` times\n- prior delayed-newer parent/child, evidence, reservation, migration, overlapping-sync, and repository-scope adversarial suites remain passing\n\n## Migration proof\n\n- used the real released `v0.7.1` schema-4 SQLite archive containing repository, PR, revision, file, and workflow-run rows\n- opened that archive through `399248c`: schema advanced from `4` to `10`, `pragma integrity_check` returned `ok`, foreign-key violations were `0`, and all seeded rows survived\n- compared complete ordered `sqlite_schema` output from the migrated archive with a fresh schema-10 archive; the diff was `0` bytes and both hashes were `9ad99a8aca9ba72ad582b9ffa6000f98edb549d093df8d92770f36c350ed397c`\n- verified the migrated schema carries source-revision ordering state for accepted evidence, every thread child family, and repository/head-SHA workflow reservations\n- the final repair adds no schema or generated-query changes; final-head sqlc generation is clean\n\n## Review closeout\n\n- equal workflow observation tuples are content-aware: subset-first then superset retains the superset, while superset-first then subset cannot delete a live run\n- same-head sibling workflow observations validated against the same baseline are consolidated before apply; exact-404 tombstones win in either persistence order\n- workflow validation now captures the exact reservation and stored rows it inspected, then compare-and-applies that state inside the persistence transaction\n- a stale snapshot with a higher local sequence is rejected when a 404-verified deletion changes the commit-time snapshot, preventing resurrection\n- workflow rows missing both `created_at` and `updated_at` fail closed for incoming collections, exact-run verification, and stored snapshots\n- PR-detail archive freshness compares child reservations with accepted evidence source/sequence, not a newer metadata-only parent observation\n- equal-tuple per-run conflicts fail closed; only compatible newer members or missing members are merged\n- prior foreign-key rollback, malformed-schema, minimum-int64, and freshness-predicate findings remain regression-covered\n- final-head GitHub checks and independent review are required before merge",
